BEFORE YOU START — TWO THINGS TO ALWAYS KNOW
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The node structure:

struct ListNode {
    int val;
    ListNode* next;
};
THE DUMMY NODE TRICK — use it on almost every problem.
Create a dummy node before the head. It eliminates edge cases
for inserting or removing at the head.

ListNode dummy(0);
dummy.next = head;
ListNode* cur = &dummy;

// ... manipulate list ...

return dummy.next;   // new head
