TYPE 2 — REVERSAL
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When to use:
→ Reverse the entire list
→ Reverse a sublist (from position l to r)
→ Reverse in groups of k

The core reversal — memorize this:

ListNode* prev = nullptr;
ListNode* cur  = head;

while (cur) {
    ListNode* next = cur->next;   // 1. save next
    cur->next = prev;             // 2. reverse pointer
    prev = cur;                   // 3. advance prev
    cur = next;                   // 4. advance cur
}
return prev;   // new head
EXAMPLE — Reverse Linked List
https://leetcode.com/problems/reverse-linked-list

Directly apply the template.

ListNode* reverseList(ListNode* head) {
    ListNode* prev = nullptr, *cur = head;
    while (cur) {
        ListNode* next = cur->next;
        cur->next = prev;
        prev = cur;
        cur = next;
    }
    return prev;
}
EXAMPLE — Reverse Linked List II (positions l to r)
https://leetcode.com/problems/reverse-linked-list-ii

Step 1: Walk to the node just before position l.
Step 2: Repeatedly move the node after cur to the front of the sublist.

ListNode* reverseBetween(ListNode* head, int l, int r) {
    ListNode dummy(0);
    dummy.next = head;
    ListNode* prev_node = &dummy;

    for (int i = 1; i < l; i++)
        prev_node = prev_node->next;

    ListNode* cur = prev_node->next;
    for (int i = 0; i < r - l; i++) {
        ListNode* next = cur->next;
        cur->next = next->next;
        next->next = prev_node->next;
        prev_node->next = next;
    }
    return dummy.next;
}
EXAMPLE — Reverse Nodes in k-Group (Hard)
https://leetcode.com/problems/reverse-nodes-in-k-group

Reverse every k nodes. Leave remaining nodes (fewer than k) as is.
Step 1: Check if at least k nodes remain.
Step 2: Reverse the next k nodes.
Step 3: Recursively apply to the rest.
After reversing, head becomes the tail — connect it to the recursive result.

ListNode* reverseKGroup(ListNode* head, int k) {
    ListNode* cur = head;
    int count = 0;
    while (cur && count < k) { cur = cur->next; count++; }
    if (count < k) return head;   // fewer than k nodes remain

    ListNode* prev = nullptr, *node = head;
    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {
        ListNode* next = node->next;
        node->next = prev;
        prev = node;
        node = next;
    }
    head->next = reverseKGroup(node, k);
    return prev;
}
