TYPE 4 — NODE REARRANGEMENT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When to use:
→ Reorder nodes based on index or value
→ Split the list into parts and rejoin in a different order
→ Deep copy a list with extra pointers

General approach: split into sub-lists → manipulate each → merge.

EXAMPLE — Odd Even Linked List
https://leetcode.com/problems/odd-even-linked-list

Separate odd-indexed and even-indexed nodes into two chains.
Connect the tail of the odd chain to the head of the even chain.

ListNode* oddEvenList(ListNode* head) {
    if (!head) return head;
    ListNode* odd = head, *even = head->next, *evenHead = even;
    while (even && even->next) {
        odd->next  = even->next;  odd  = odd->next;
        even->next = odd->next;   even = even->next;
    }
    odd->next = evenHead;
    return head;
}
EXAMPLE — Reorder List
https://leetcode.com/problems/reorder-list

Given: 1→2→3→4→5, produce: 1→5→2→4→3.

Step 1: Find middle (fast/slow pointers).
Step 2: Reverse the second half.
Step 3: Merge the two halves alternately.

void reorderList(ListNode* head) {
    ListNode* slow = head, *fast = head;
    while (fast->next && fast->next->next) {
        slow = slow->next;
        fast = fast->next->next;
    }
    // reverse second half
    ListNode* prev = nullptr, *cur = slow->next;
    slow->next = nullptr;   // cut the list in half
    while (cur) {
        ListNode* next = cur->next;
        cur->next = prev;
        prev = cur;
        cur = next;
    }
    // merge alternately
    ListNode* l1 = head, *l2 = prev;
    while (l2) {
        ListNode* next1 = l1->next, *next2 = l2->next;
        l1->next = l2;
        l2->next = next1;
        l1 = next1;
        l2 = next2;
    }
}
EXAMPLE — Partition List
https://leetcode.com/problems/partition-list

Build two separate chains: nodes < x, and nodes >= x.
Connect the tail of the less chain to the head of the greater chain.

ListNode* partition(ListNode* head, int x) {
    ListNode lessHead(0), greaterHead(0);
    ListNode* less = &lessHead, *greater = &greaterHead;
    while (head) {
        if (head->val < x) { less->next = head; less = less->next; }
        else { greater->next = head; greater = greater->next; }
        head = head->next;
    }
    greater->next = nullptr;
    less->next = greaterHead.next;
    return lessHead.next;
}
EXAMPLE — Copy List with Random Pointer
https://leetcode.com/problems/copy-list-with-random-pointer

Each node has val, next, and random (can point anywhere).

Step 1: Build a hashmap {original node → cloned node}.
Step 2: Set next and random on each clone using the map.

Node* copyRandomList(Node* head) {
    unordered_map<Node*, Node*> mp;
    Node* cur = head;
    while (cur) { mp[cur] = new Node(cur->val); cur = cur->next; }
    cur = head;
    while (cur) {
        mp[cur]->next   = mp[cur->next];
        mp[cur]->random = mp[cur->random];
        cur = cur->next;
    }
    return mp[head];
}
